  S.outputs.push(
    {id:'P-001',type:'P',title:'Signpost every alternative route',title_zh:'给每条备选路线立路标',advice:'If a route is meant to be an easier path, show it from where the hard path begins.',advice_zh:'如果一条路线是作为更容易的路径设计的，就在困难路径的起点让玩家看见它。',why:'Players read an unseen alternative as "no alternative". Difficulty they cannot route around feels unfair even when the design offered a way out.',why_zh:'玩家把看不见的备选读成"没有备选"。绕不过去的难度即使设计上留了出口，也会被感受为不公平。',how:'Put a vantage point, map marker or NPC line at the decision point. Playtest by asking testers to list the routes they believe exist — compare with the routes you built.',how_zh:'在决策点放一个观景点、地图标记或 NPC 台词。测试时让玩家列出他们以为存在的路线，和你建的路线对比。',evidence:['SUB-20260901-001.2','SUB-20260901-001.3','SUB-20260901-002.1'],claims:['C-001'],mechanisms:['implicit-path'],audience:'Small teams building open or semi-open levels',audience_zh:'做开放或半开放关卡的小团队',status:'published',created:'2026-09-06'},
    {id:'W-001',type:'W',title:"Don't call your own easy mode 'not the real game'",title_zh:'别把你自己的简单模式叫"不是真正的游戏"',advice:'Never label an assist or mode as the un-intended experience inside your own UI.',advice_zh:'永远不要在自己的界面里把辅助或模式标注为"非本意的体验"。',why:'The label, not the assist, is what mastery-oriented players react to. It converts a helpful option into a badge of shame, and some stuck players will refuse it.',why_zh:'精通导向的玩家反应的是标签，不是辅助本身。标签把有用的选项变成耻辱徽章，一部分卡关的玩家会拒绝使用。',how:'Describe what the mode changes, not who it is for. If you must state intent, put it in a dev note or blog, not on the toggle.',how_zh:'描述模式改变了什么，而不是它给谁用。如果一定要表达意图，放在开发者说明或博客里，别放在开关上。',evidence:['SUB-20260903-003.2','SUB-20260903-003.3'],claims:['C-002'],mechanisms:['difficulty-modes','in-game-assists'],audience:'Any team shipping an easy mode or assist',audience_zh:'任何要上简单模式或辅助的团队',status:'published',created:'2026-09-06'},
    {id:'F-001',type:'F',title:'Which difficulty lever fits my game?',title_zh:'哪个难度杠杆适合我的游戏？',advice:'Three questions about structure, feeling and team size, scored against every mechanism\'s fit tags and published evidence.',advice_zh:'关于结构、感受和团队规模的三个问题，对每个机制的适配标签和已发布证据打分。',why:'Most small teams reach for a difficulty menu by default. The right lever depends on structure, the feeling you are protecting, and how much tuning you can afford.',why_zh:'大多数小团队默认伸手去拿难度菜单。合适的杠杆取决于结构、你要保护的感受，以及你负担得起多少调试。',how:'Answer the questions on the Advisor page. Each result links to the mechanism page and the evidence behind it.',how_zh:'在顾问页回答问题。每个结果都链接到机制页和背后的证据。',evidence:[],claims:['C-001','C-002'],mechanisms:['difficulty-modes','implicit-path','failure-cost','in-game-assists'],audience:'Developers at concept or prototype stage',audience_zh:'概念或原型阶段的开发者',status:'published',created:'2026-09-07'},
    {id:'P-002',type:'P',title:'Name the adaptive system somewhere players can find it',title_zh:'把自适应系统写在玩家找得到的地方',advice:'If the game adjusts to the player, say so — in a codex entry, a loading tip, or the options screen.',advice_zh:'如果游戏会随玩家调整，就说出来——图鉴条目、加载提示或选项页都行。',why:'Discovery from outside the game turns a clever system into a suspicion that the game was staging moments.',why_zh:'从游戏外得知，会把一个聪明的系统变成"游戏在演戏"的怀疑。',how:'One sentence is enough. You do not have to explain the model, only that it exists and what it is for.',how_zh:'一句话就够。不必解释模型，只说它存在、为了什么。',evidence:['SUB-20260905-004.1','SUB-20260905-004.2'],claims:['C-003'],mechanisms:['ai-director'],audience:'Teams building adaptive pacing or spawning',audience_zh:'做自适应节奏或刷怪的团队',status:'draft',created:'2026-09-08'}
  );
  S.posts.push({id:'POST-001',date:'2026-09-10',status:'published',title:'Why this library treats difficulty as a negotiation',title_zh:'为什么这个库把难度当作一场协商',body:'Most difficulty advice starts from the menu: how many modes, which sliders. This library starts one step earlier — with the moment a player meets a challenge and decides what to do about it: push through, look for another way, open a guide, install a mod, or quit.\n\nThat decision is where difficulty actually lives. The mechanism is only the opening offer; the player answers with behaviour; the community answers with guides and patches; the developer answers back with the next update. Every mechanism page here is organised around that back-and-forth, and every principle is published only when several independent people describe the same negotiation.\n\nThe first batches will come from students analysing games they know well. If you teach, the instructor note explains how to take part without touching grading.',body_zh:'大多数难度建议从菜单开始：几档、哪些滑块。这个库往前退一步——从玩家遇到挑战、决定怎么办的那一刻开始：硬打、找别的路、开攻略、装模组，或者退出。\n\n那个决定才是难度真正存在的地方。机制只是开价；玩家用行为回应；社区用攻略和补丁回应；开发者用下一次更新再回应。这里的每一个机制页都围绕这一来一回组织，每一条原则只有在几个独立的人描述了同一种协商之后才发布。\n\n第一批数据会来自分析自己熟悉的游戏的学生。如果你是教师，教师说明解释了如何在不触碰评分的前提下参与。',refs:['implicit-path','P-001']});
  S.postIdeas.push({id:'IDEA-001',date:'2026-09-06',text:'The label problem (C-002) is really a UX-copy problem — write a post on the words games use for their own easy modes.',source:'C-002'});
